:[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Decomposition/certification checkpoint (2026-08-17): RP-03 depends_on RP-02 citric-moudly-vipersquid. Story order is S1 stable-foggy-hammerkop -> S2 unrational-undefiled-shoveler -> S3 slowmoving-engaging-kouprey -> S4 vegan-defaceable-moth -> S5 diamond-flavoured-esok, with S5 also directly depending on S1. S1's contract leaf heavensent-nonproift-galago and parent stable-foggy-hammerkop are certified PASS/current at origin/main 034e17209c. next-batch returns only that already-certified contract leaf. This epic intentionally remains unsigned while its RP-02 blocker is open; blocked descendants were not force-reviewed or claimed.","timestamp":1787034269928791001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision (2026-08-19) — cross-cutting constraint folded into this epic's S5 line.\n\nTicket `insectile-modest-martin` (d7b9-ac42) has been CLOSED and its requirement folded directly\ninto the acceptance criteria of `diamond-flavoured-esok` (RP-03 S5) and `postmodern-tangled-mollusk`\n(RP-03 S5 T2), so the constraint travels with the work that can actually violate it.\n\nWhy it moved: martin was a standalone guard ticket protecting an ordering invariant in\n`reconcile.py` during an extraction that had not yet happened. A guard that lands AFTER the\nextraction can only DETECT a break; folded into the tickets performing the extraction, it PREVENTS\none. The failure mode is silent — the repair still runs and still writes correct-looking bytes when\nmis-ordered — which is exactly the class of requirement that must not sit in a separate ticket\nsomeone might schedule later.\n\nThe constraint in one line: `binding_store.repair_at_write_boundary(...)` must stay AFTER the\nunder-lock staleness gate (`ensure_selection_current`) and BEFORE the pass's first remote issue\nfetch. `reconcile.py` is at 799/800 lines, so S5 must extract along an existing call-graph seam\nwithout raising the cap, and must RE-ANCHOR (never relax) the two boundary tests in\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_recovery_write_boundary.py. Full text and the inherited\nacceptance criteria are in both children's descriptions; the rationale is in ADR 0099.","timestamp":1787174009364435001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Added a REQUIRED epic AC: a green Live External Integration GitHub Actions run exercising the coordinator/create/fuse end-to-end against BOTH live Jira Cloud and live Jira DC (real transports+credentials, not fakes). Per operator directive, the epic must not close until this live run passes. This makes slice-5's 'bounded live validation' an explicit, gated close criterion.","timestamp":1787695424075733001}],"created_at":1787022393777304001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"03ba0e00-01fb-4aba-9a03-42322d827293","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"5e64-d9cd-2dd4-4036"},{"link_uuid":"a0461f9e-df7e-42ec-b08b-f278d7e2bdda","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"10c8-9981-3877-4ed5"},{"link_uuid":"d6b76bf3-6ad4-4893-88b3-57986a840e47","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9b75-8bb5-601d-402d"},{"link_uuid":"8af187f7-2dd8-43ff-90f8-0fb97230e106","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ee98-a2c0-7d12-4c75"},{"link_uuid":"c7e0dc26-1abd-4a0b-95e4-ff6e1c9d3e94","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"decb-e486-dfeb-48fd"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nRebar currently decides and performs Jira work across the differ, generic apply wrapper, Cloud ACLI/REST, Jira DC SDK, handlers, and batch orchestration. Retry ownership is multiplied: one logical postcondition can cross nested loops, whole compound updates can replay after a late failure, provider delay can be capped and retried early, and terminal failures do not have a stable per-ticket versus batch scope. No existing mechanism models these outcomes: the reconciler's only breaker (`classify.check_blast_radius`) is a per-pass blast-radius acting-fraction guard against mass mutation, not an endpoint-failure fuse.\n\n## Outcome\nBuild one provider-neutral coordinator around immutable observation and pure per-ticket `TicketPlan` values. Each plan carries existing `Mutation` values, lifecycle intents, dependencies, diagnostics, and disposition. Global selection/filter/caps run before any lifecycle or remote effect. Concrete adapters own physical replay, timeouts, cleanup, SDK retry disablement, and provider decoding; core owns commit-unknown recovery, re-observation/replanning, dependency deferral, the finite-pass fuse, and exact ticket/pass outcomes.\n\n## Approved policy\n- At most three physical invocations and 15 seconds cumulative sleep per logical postcondition, including one observe/replan cycle; fallback delays are approximately 2s then 4s with nonnegative jitter.\n- `Retry-After` or equivalent is a lower bound. If it cannot fit, return `retry_not_before` for a later pass rather than retrying early.\n- Add a new endpoint-failure scoped fuse (none exists today; the reconciler has no rolling/consecutive failure-rate breaker). An endpoint family opens after three consecutive exhausted eligible logical outcomes across at least two tickets. Provider scope additionally requires two endpoint families. Matching success resets the scope. Attempts, recovered warnings, permanent failures, and opaque diagnostics do not count. The existing per-pass blast-radius acting-fraction guard (`classify.check_blast_radius`) is a distinct mass-mutation protection and is RETAINED unchanged; the fuse adds endpoint-failure protection and does not remove blast-radius protection.\n- Authoritative credential, configuration, quota, rate, issue, endpoint, tenant, and global scopes retain their direct classified behavior.\n- Create containment is label-first (`rebar-id:<local_id>`), optional property second, then safety-abort with the known key if local persistence fails.\n\n## Delivery slices\n1. Prove one Cloud/DC operation end to end through normalized outcomes and the single retry budget with deterministic fake transports.\n2. Produce immutable shadow plans and versioned preview lifecycle intents from one observation with zero remote/local effects.\n3. Cut non-create operations to the coordinator with dependency deferral, exact partial outcomes, retry deferral, and scoped fuse.\n4. Cut create and lifecycle recovery to the RP-02 transaction seam with commit-unknown containment.\n5. Finish expand/contract cutover, remove legacy retry/write fallbacks, and seal manifests, observability, cursor behavior, documentation, and bounded live validation.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nShadow planning first compares existing mutation shape and provider-neutral outcomes without writes. Cutover is by operation family and never dual-writes. Before contract removal, an operation can return to the legacy dispatcher. Rollback never deletes a successful Jira effect; commit-unknown work is re-observed. Existing ticket/event/binding shapes remain readable, and preview adds versioned lifecycle intent fields without changing the existing mutation shape.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] One observation deterministically produces per-ticket plans whose selection, caps, dependencies, diagnostics, dispositions, mutations, and lifecycle intents are testable without Jira or filesystem writes.\n- [ ] Cloud ACLI/REST and Jira DC execute each logical postcondition within one three-call/15-second budget, disable hidden SDK retry, honor provider lower bounds, and defer long waits with `retry_not_before`.\n- [ ] The riskiest DC capability — that the real Jira DC SDK honors `max_retries=0` by exposing `_session.max_retries == 0` — is proven in-session in S1 against the actual `jira` 3.10.5 library via an offline construction test (no network/credentials), not only via fake transports.\n- [ ] The coordinator classifies auto-healed, retryable, permanent, commit-unknown, ticket-local, endpoint, tenant, provider, and global outcomes with exact per-ticket and pass tallies.\n- [ ] The approved three-consecutive scoped fuse triggers only from normalized exhausted logical outcomes and does not stop historically successful/partially successful replay fixtures prematurely.\n- [ ] Create tests prove label-first containment, optional property enrichment, known-key safety-abort, and no duplicate create after timeout or persistence failure.\n- [ ] Shadow/cutover tests prove no dual-write, safe fallback before legacy removal, versioned preview compatibility, fail-loud unsupported production paths, and no rollback deletion of successful Jira work.\n- [ ] A **Live External Integration** workflow runs GREEN in GitHub Actions, fully exercising this epic's coordinator, create/binding-lifecycle, commit-unknown recovery, and endpoint/provider fuse functionality end-to-end against BOTH a live **Jira Cloud** instance and a live **Jira Data Center** instance (real transports and credentials, not deterministic fakes). This live run is a REQUIRED gate: the epic MUST NOT be closed until it has passed.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/operation_outcome.py","reason":"Provider-neutral operation outcomes."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/retry_budget.py","reason":"Single physical retry budget."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/observation.py","reason":"Immutable pass observation."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/ticket_plan.py","reason":"Per-ticket plan and lifecycle intents."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/ticket_planner.py","reason":"Pure plan construction."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/coordinator.py","reason":"Typed execution and recovery coordination."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/failure_policy.py","reason":"Failure taxonomy and blast-radius decisions."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/pass_fuse.py","reason":"Scoped finite-pass fuse."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py","reason":"Coordinator cutover and legacy path removal."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/manifest_renderer.py","reason":"Versioned preview and outcome observability."},{"path":"docs/adr/0103-reconciler-operation-coordination.md","reason":"Architecture, retry, fuse, and cutover record."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_coordinator.py","reason":"Portable end-to-end Cloud/DC evidence."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","5e64-d9cd-2dd4-4036"],["relates_to","9b75-8bb5-601d-402d"],["relates_to","decb-e486-dfeb-48fd"],["relates_to","ee98-a2c0-7d12-4c75"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"b5ad43ea-c9b0-468f-9dcd-0998e3c6e837","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor","rp03","reconciler","jira","reliability"],"ticket_id":"4217-d1d6-370b-4e98","ticket_type":"epic","title":"RP-03 — Coordinate Jira mutations with typed plans, bounded retry, and scoped fuse","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_ticket_plan_shadow.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_operation_retry_budget.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_scoped_pass_fuse.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC4","dd_text":"Planning, retry budget, taxonomy, and scoped fuse contract"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_create_operation_coordinator.py","dd_id":"AC5","dd_text":"Create containment and duplicate-prevention contract"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_coordinator.py","dd_id":"AC6","dd_text":"Portable no-dual-write Cloud/DC cutover validation"}]},"source_event_uuids":["d3a4be63-cb8e-4a97-89f0-6bcf071d5fa7","042ceff2-ae4d-41e0-aad7-5f82ab5ecfce","c7e0dc26-1abd-4a0b-95e4-ff6e1c9d3e94","141f82e0-8061-489b-b1dd-f760dfe21480","8a4492ea-d213-4484-9444-0901d6f4f01a","c964aefa-b212-4f21-88cc-b9a1508b520e","b5ad43ea-c9b0-468f-9dcd-0998e3c6e837","7712bc44-6608-4772-b118-e4ca0870d65b","ebefb85d-0ec7-477a-a21b-1e0d3f71728e","effd5664-8de6-4dd8-a42d-a932ca86bf98","360531ce-fed3-47da-bb13-d9d5bf33e724"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787713796734212001,"uuid":"d2c46576-003e-4055-8318-14797dba57aa"}